# Independently versioned lines in one repository (a monorepo). Each
# [[packages]] entry is a subtree with its own tag line (<path>/vX.Y.Z — the
# Go multi-module rule, not configurable), its own walk base and its own
# rolling draft. A commit moves the lines its files lie under (a nested
# package takes its files out of its parent); a commit touching no package's
# files may name one in its scope, and with a version sigil MUST. Leave this
# out for one version line, which is what every repository has without it.
# A verdict input wherever a diff can be read — bump, notes, release,
# preview --pr, lint --range, the pre-push hook — and the reusable
# release.yml answers per line through its `packages` output
# (docs/DESIGN.md §4.1).
#
# [[packages]]
# path = "haiku"          # tags haiku/vX.Y.Z; a scope calls it (haiku)
#
# [[packages]]
# path = "."              # the root package: bare vX.Y.Z, and every file no
# name = "core"           # other package claims; a scope calls it (core)
